1
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:05,422
Hey, out of all of us

2
00:00:05,464 --> 00:00:07,549
who do you think's going
to get married next?

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:12,137
Probably Monica
and Chandler.

4
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:18,352
Hi, could I have a pack
of Newport Lights, please?

5
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:20,354
Uh, we don't sell cigarettes,
but they have them

6
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:21,814
at the newsstand
across the street.

7
00:00:21,856 --> 00:00:23,983
That'd be great. Thanks.

8
00:00:26,318 --> 00:00:27,569
Oh, my God.

9
00:00:27,611 --> 00:00:28,946
Melissa Warburton.

10
00:00:28,988 --> 00:00:30,531
I don't think I have the energy
for this.

11
00:00:30,572 --> 00:00:31,824
( theatrical gasp )

12
00:00:31,866 --> 00:00:33,074
Oh, my God.

13
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,326
Ray-Ray Green?

14
00:00:34,368 --> 00:00:35,536
( screaming )

15
00:00:36,829 --> 00:00:37,955
Melissa!

16
00:00:37,997 --> 00:00:39,247
( laughing )

17
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:41,249
You have been MIA

18
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:43,627
for the past seven
sorority newsletters.

19
00:00:43,669 --> 00:00:44,795
What's up with you?

20
00:00:44,837 --> 00:00:46,005
( laughing ):
Well...

21
00:00:46,045 --> 00:00:48,215
Why don't I tell you over here?

22
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:54,513
So, last I heard,
you were going to get married.

23
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:56,181
Oh... poor Ray-Ray.

24
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:57,432
Oh, no, no, no.

25
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:58,934
That's good;
it's all good.

26
00:00:58,976 --> 00:01:00,769
I actually work
at Ralph Lauren.

27
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:02,062
Shut up!

28
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:03,564
I will not.

29
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:06,316
I'm the Divisional Head
of Men's Sportswear.

30
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:07,818
Oh, shut up more!

31
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:10,195
Are you friends with Ralph?

32
00:01:10,237 --> 00:01:11,947
Oh, please.

33
00:01:11,989 --> 00:01:12,865
Are you?

34
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:14,449
No.

35
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:15,826
Listen

36
00:01:15,868 --> 00:01:17,160
we-we have to have dinner.

37
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:18,871
What are you doing
tomorrow night?

38
00:01:18,913 --> 00:01:20,706
Oh, tomorrow, I...
I don't know. Um...

39
00:01:20,748 --> 00:01:22,708
You're having dinner
with me.

40
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:25,168
Shut up.

41
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:26,378
I've got to go.

42
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:28,547
This has been
so great, Ray-Ray.

43
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:29,798
Oh, there you are.

44
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:32,133
Um, so, listen,
just call me.

45
00:01:32,175 --> 00:01:33,385
Here's my card.

46
00:01:33,427 --> 00:01:34,720
Oh, wow, thanks.

47
00:01:34,762 --> 00:01:36,513
Oh, you're in real estate.

48
00:01:36,555 --> 00:01:38,724
Oh, no, that's...
that's an old card.

49
00:01:38,766 --> 00:01:41,560
Um, I wanted to
get out of that
and do something

50
00:01:41,602 --> 00:01:43,478
where I could
really help people

51
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,855
and make a difference.

52
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:46,648
Wow. So, what do you do now?

53
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:48,901
I'm a party planner.

54
00:01:48,943 --> 00:01:51,152
I'll see
you tomorrow.

55
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:52,529
Okay.

56
00:01:52,571 --> 00:01:55,407
Hey, guys,
look who's back.

57
00:01:55,449 --> 00:01:56,867
It's Ray-Ray.

58
00:01:56,909 --> 00:02:00,788
That was my friend Melissa
from college.

59
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:03,832
She seems really, really fun!

60
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:08,253
She's actually very sweet,
and we used to be very close.

61
00:02:08,295 --> 00:02:09,546
Wait a minute.

62
00:02:09,588 --> 00:02:13,300
She isn't... she's
not the one who you...?

63
00:02:13,341 --> 00:02:15,719
Who you what? Who you what?

64
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:17,512
Yes.

65
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:18,931
Wow.

66
00:02:18,973 --> 00:02:20,140
Wow-wow what? Wow what?

67
00:02:20,181 --> 00:02:21,516
Who you what?!

68
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:23,978
Oh, it's not a big deal.

69
00:02:24,019 --> 00:02:25,395
They were lovers.

70
00:02:25,437 --> 00:02:27,272
What?
What?

71
00:02:27,314 --> 00:02:28,523
No, we weren't.

72
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:29,775
It was nothing.

73
00:02:29,817 --> 00:02:32,152
It was one night senior year.

74
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:33,946
We went to a party...

75
00:02:33,988 --> 00:02:37,825
had a lot of sangria,
and, you know, ended up...

76
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:39,868
kissing for a bit.

77
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:42,704
So, that's two of my wives.

78
00:02:49,795 --> 00:02:54,842
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

79
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:57,302
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

80
00:02:57,344 --> 00:02:59,638
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

81
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:04,309
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

82
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:07,813
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

83
00:03:07,855 --> 00:03:09,898
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

84
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:13,192
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

85
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:16,655
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

86
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:29,084
Okay, so, this
is where the band is

87
00:03:29,126 --> 00:03:31,586
and this is where the bar is,
and all these pins

88
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:34,089
have people's names on them.

89
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:35,423
Rach, here you are.

90
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:36,675
Oh, wow.

91
00:03:36,717 --> 00:03:38,552
Well, why don't we
just take me

92
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:40,929
and put me
with a Manhattan in my hand

93
00:03:40,971 --> 00:03:42,764
talking to the cute bartender?

94
00:03:42,806 --> 00:03:44,141
( chuckling )

95
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:49,312
These pins aren't for playing,
are they?

96
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:53,274
Okay, the red ones are my guests
and the blue pins are yours.

97
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:54,651
This is so sad.

98
00:03:54,693 --> 00:03:56,987
I mean, I only have,
like, ten pins.

99
00:03:57,029 --> 00:03:58,072
Chandler, relax.

100
00:03:58,113 --> 00:03:59,322
It's not a contest.

101
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:01,366
It's certainly not
a close one.

102
00:04:02,993 --> 00:04:04,285
Hello.

103
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:05,412
Hey.

104
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:10,500
Hey, Rach.

105
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:13,962
Stop picturing it!

106
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:18,133
Okay, I think that's it.

107
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:19,927
The seating chart is done.

108
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,511
This is our wedding.

109
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:25,140
Wow. They all look like
they're having fun, don't they?

110
00:04:25,182 --> 00:04:27,184
Hey, so, where are my parents
going to be?

111
00:04:27,226 --> 00:04:30,520
Oh, let's see, well, if
this is the wedding hall

112
00:04:30,562 --> 00:04:32,689
then, um, your
parents would be

113
00:04:32,731 --> 00:04:35,859
over here at home in Queens.

114
00:04:35,901 --> 00:04:37,318
What? They're not invited?

115
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,653
Oh, no, that's terrible.

116
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:40,197
They're going to be crushed.

117
00:04:40,239 --> 00:04:41,823
Why would they think
they're invited?

118
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:45,660
You got me. I...

119
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:46,828
Joey...

120
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:48,205
Well, I'm sorry.

121
00:04:48,247 --> 00:04:50,540
Look, I thought parents
were coming, you know?

122
00:04:50,582 --> 00:04:53,501
Your parents are coming,
Chandler's parents are coming

123
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:54,920
Ross' parents are coming.

124
00:04:54,962 --> 00:04:57,923
Ross' parents are my parents.

125
00:04:57,965 --> 00:05:00,759
Well, see? Parents are coming.

126
00:05:02,261 --> 00:05:04,054
You know, I think
we should invite them.

127
00:05:04,096 --> 00:05:06,140
Oh, please.
You just want more blue pins.

128
00:05:06,181 --> 00:05:07,724
Well, this is just sad.

129
00:05:07,766 --> 00:05:09,601
All right,
all right.

130
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:11,645
Maybe I can
fit them in

131
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:14,355
if I just do some rearranging.

132
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:17,025
Now Rachel may actually have
to sit at the bar.

133
00:05:17,067 --> 00:05:19,736
That is not a problem.

134
00:05:19,778 --> 00:05:22,030
Maybe you'll order
a little sangria.

135
00:05:22,072 --> 00:05:23,198
Oh, get out of here!

136
00:05:27,911 --> 00:05:29,955
So, now, these are all
the tuxedos that we make

137
00:05:29,997 --> 00:05:31,581
and if there's anything
that you like

138
00:05:31,623 --> 00:05:32,666
we can make you a deal.

139
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:34,126
Anything at all.

140
00:05:34,168 --> 00:05:37,545
But these are the three
that Monica pre-approved.

141
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:40,339
Ah, well, thanks a lot
for hooking me up, Rach

142
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:42,634
and I want you to know
that I want you

143
00:05:42,676 --> 00:05:44,761
to attend our wedding
as my guest.

144
00:05:47,973 --> 00:05:50,892
I'm Monica's
maid of honor, okay?

145
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:53,103
Don't try to blue-pin me.

146
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,231
Well, what's the deal
with these?

147
00:05:56,273 --> 00:05:57,232
These look nice.

148
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:58,525
Oh, they are nice.

149
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:00,568
We, we custom-make
tuxedos for celebrities

150
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,903
and when they're
done with them

151
00:06:01,945 --> 00:06:03,030
they send them back.

152
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:05,073
You mean, like,
for awards shows?

153
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:06,116
Some of them.

154
00:06:06,158 --> 00:06:07,450
You mean these tuxes
have been

155
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:09,577
down the red carpet
with people yelling, uh

156
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:10,620
"Who are you wearing?

157
00:06:10,662 --> 00:06:11,746
You look fabulous!"

158
00:06:13,165 --> 00:06:15,250
Honey, might I
suggest watching

159
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:17,961
a little more ESPN
and a little less E?

160
00:06:19,963 --> 00:06:22,423
Okay, who wore those?

161
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:24,051
Um... well, let's see.

162
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:25,927
Uh, this one's Tom Brokaw.

163
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:27,470
Not bad.

164
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:29,931
This one is, uh,
Paul O'Neill.

165
00:06:29,973 --> 00:06:32,267
Who is that?

166
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,937
He plays for the Yankees.

167
00:06:35,979 --> 00:06:37,480
Seriously, ESPN.

168
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:38,606
Just once in a while.

169
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:40,275
Have it on in the background.

170
00:06:43,987 --> 00:06:46,073
Ooh, this one
was Pierce Brosnan.

171
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:47,074
Pierce Brosnan?

172
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:48,075
Uh-huh.

173
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,784
Are you serious? 007?

174
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:51,870
This is James Bond's tux?

175
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:55,623
Oh, I have to get married
in James Bond's tux.

176
00:06:55,665 --> 00:06:57,084
It's a pretty cool tux.

177
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,501
Ah, it's not
just that.

178
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:00,754
I would be England's
most powerful weapon.

179
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:04,216
A jet-setting
heartbreaker

180
00:07:04,258 --> 00:07:06,509
on Her Majesty's
Secret Service.

181
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:09,971
A man who fears no one,
with a license to kill.

182
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,684
Would Monica
let me wear this?

183
00:07:19,438 --> 00:07:21,524
We should really learn
how to play the real way.

184
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:25,028
No, I like our way.
Oh...

185
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,487
Ooh, ah, hey.

186
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:27,948
Chess!

187
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,701
Nice move.

188
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:32,827
Yeah.

189
00:07:32,869 --> 00:07:34,246
Hey.

190
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:35,705
Hey.
Hey.

191
00:07:35,747 --> 00:07:37,498
So, Joey, I just hooked
Ross and Chandler up

192
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:38,917
with some tuxedos
for the wedding.

193
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:40,001
Do you need one?

194
00:07:40,043 --> 00:07:41,295
No. I'm performing
the ceremony.

195
00:07:41,336 --> 00:07:42,296
I'm not wearing a tux.

196
00:07:42,337 --> 00:07:43,630
What are you going to wear?

197
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:45,340
Multi-colored robes.

198
00:07:45,382 --> 00:07:47,217
Ooh, and maybe a hat.

199
00:07:47,259 --> 00:07:48,343
Huh.

200
00:07:48,385 --> 00:07:49,761
Does Monica know about this?

201
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:50,929
I don't think so.

202
00:07:50,971 --> 00:07:52,347
Can I be there
when you tell her?

203
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:56,893
Hey, oh, Rach, wait.

204
00:07:56,935 --> 00:07:58,312
Do you want to go
to a movie tonight?

205
00:07:58,353 --> 00:08:00,772
I have to have dinner
with that Melissa girl.

206
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:02,065
Can I come?

207
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:05,277
I won't even talk.

208
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:07,028
You'll just hear the noise
from my video camera.

209
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:08,780
What is this?
What's going on?

210
00:08:08,822 --> 00:08:10,157
Can I tell her, can I tell her?

211
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:11,866
Do you want to hear
what actually happened

212
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:12,867
or Joey's lewd version?

213
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:13,868
Joey's.

214
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,329
Okay.

215
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:16,579
No, hey, come on.

216
00:08:16,621 --> 00:08:18,873
I have this friend from college

217
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:22,210
and I made the stupid mistake
of telling Joey

218
00:08:22,252 --> 00:08:25,046
that one time...
she and I, you know...

219
00:08:25,088 --> 00:08:26,547
kissed a little bit.

220
00:08:26,589 --> 00:08:27,924
( chuckling )

221
00:08:27,966 --> 00:08:29,884
Yeah, I'm sure that happened.

222
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:32,511
It... it did.

223
00:08:32,553 --> 00:08:33,763
Sure.

224
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:38,685
Hey, it happened.

225
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:43,190
Yeah, it was senior year
in college.

226
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:45,566
It was after the Sigma Chi luau

227
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:47,944
and Melissa and I
got very drunk

228
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:49,946
and we ended up kissing...

229
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:51,531
for several minutes.

230
00:08:51,572 --> 00:08:53,408
Which means she had
a couple spritzers

231
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:55,035
and a quick peck on the cheek.

232
00:08:56,495 --> 00:08:58,413
Why are you taking this
away from me?

233
00:08:59,998 --> 00:09:02,501
Yeah, why is it
so hard for you to believe?

234
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:06,296
Okay, I just, I
didn't know that
you were lesbian.

235
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:15,389
I'm not saying
that I am a lesbian.

236
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:18,058
I'm just saying
that this happened.

237
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:20,768
Okay. It just
seems pretty wild

238
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,980
and you're, you
know, so... vanilla.

239
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:25,440
( muffled squeak )

240
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:27,442
Vanilla? I'm not vanilla.

241
00:09:27,484 --> 00:09:29,944
I've done lots of crazy things.

242
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:33,198
I mean, I got drunk and married
in Vegas.

243
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:35,283
To Ross.

244
00:09:35,325 --> 00:09:36,659
All right, you know what?

245
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,245
If you don't want to believe me
about this

246
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:40,414
why don't you just come with me
to dinner tonight

247
00:09:40,455 --> 00:09:41,540
and she will tell you.

248
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:42,665
Okay.

249
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:43,791
All right, yeah.

250
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:46,002
'Cause I just can't picture it.

251
00:09:46,044 --> 00:09:48,422
Oh, you should get
inside my head.

252
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,010
Hey.

253
00:09:54,052 --> 00:09:55,887
Guess what I got
for your wedding?

254
00:09:55,929 --> 00:09:58,639
A freakishly thin date
with a hanger for a head?

255
00:09:59,891 --> 00:10:02,269
No, Rachel hooked me up
with a tux.

256
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:03,811
But not just any tux.

257
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:05,855
Batman's tux.

258
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:07,148
What?

259
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:08,483
That's right.

260
00:10:08,525 --> 00:10:10,610
Made expressly for Val Kilmer

261
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:13,029
and worn by him
in the hit film...

262
00:10:13,071 --> 00:10:15,823
that Batman film he was in.

263
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:17,200
You can't wear that.

264
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:19,035
I'm wearing the famous tux--
James Bond's tux.

265
00:10:19,077 --> 00:10:20,703
So?

266
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:24,541
So, if you wear that,
it'll make mine less special.

267
00:10:24,583 --> 00:10:27,085
